.TH CIRCQ_TRY_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
circq_try_send_zc \- try to send without blocking
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t circq_try_send_zc(circular_queue *cq, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Attempts to send immediately. If the queue is full, returns immediately
with ccol_container_full. On success, transfers ownership of msg->data.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq   Circular queue to send to
msg  Message to send (data ownership transfers on success)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - Message sent successfully
ccol_invalid_args    - cq or msg is NULL, or msg validation fails
ccol_not_permitted   - Sending has been disabled
ccol_container_full  - Queue is full
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Never blocks
On failure, caller retains ownership of msg->data
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR circq_send_zc (3),
.BR circq_timed_send_zc (3)
